      "id": "complete",
      "title": "The response is sent only once execution is complete",
      "level": "MUST",
      "spec": [
        {
          "number": "6.3.1",
          "title": "Executing the Root Selection Set",
          "url": "https://spec.graphql.org/draft/#sec-Executing-the-Root-Selection-Set"
        },
        {
          "number": "6.3.3",
          "title": "Executing Collected Fields",
          "url": "https://spec.graphql.org/draft/#sec-Executing-Collected-Fields"
        },
        {
          "number": "7.1.5",
          "title": "Data",
          "url": "https://spec.graphql.org/draft/#sec-Data"
        }
      ],
      "basis": "No sentence says to respond only once execution is complete; the algorithms do. ExecuteRootSelectionSet (§6.3.1) returns {data} once ExecuteCollectedFields has run, and §6.3.3 says \"Execution will recursively resolve and complete the value of every entry in the collected fields map\". The draft's §7.1.5 adds: \"The response data is the result of accumulating the resolved result of all response positions during execution.\" Positions §6.3.3 lets an implementation cancel don't hold the response back.",
      "status": "pass",
      "cases": 2704,
      "failing": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "dataMatches",
      "title": "data is the completed value: field collection, value completion and null propagation",
      "level": "MUST",
      "spec": [
        {
          "number": "6.3.2",
          "title": "Field Collection",
          "url": "https://spec.graphql.org/draft/#sec-Field-Collection"
