        },
        {
          "number": "6.4.4",
          "title": "Handling Execution Errors",
          "url": "https://spec.graphql.org/draft/#sec-Handling-Execution-Errors"
        }
      ],
      "basis": "When an error propagates to the root, §6.4.4 and §7.1.5 say data \"should be null\", in both editions. The kit still requires null, because no other value conforms: the execution result must have a data entry (§7.1.1), {} or a partial map leaves out an entry ExecuteCollectedFields must produce (§6.3.3), and a map with null at the failed root field breaks that field's Non-Null type.",
      "status": "pass",
      "cases": 2704,
      "failing": 0
