    {
      "id": "disabledPropagation",
      "title": "With error propagation off, an error nulls the position where it happened (graphql-js 17's @experimental_disableErrorPropagation)",
      "level": "INFO",
      "spec": [],
      "basis": "Not a GraphQL rule: neither edition has execution without error propagation. §6.4.4 says: \"Since Non-Null response positions cannot be null, execution errors are propagated to be handled by the parent response position.\" Every failure of the noPropagation fixture's response (its data and errors) counts here, never against a spec section, and never fails the run. Turning propagation off doesn't change which resolvers run, so protocol problems and the checks on calls (callsOnce, callsSelected, callsReachable, calledSerially) keep their own checks.",
